# Database & Custom Tables (ADR-005, ADR-018)

## Source of Truth Split

- Commerce data (products, orders, customers, taxes, shipping): WooCommerce +
  HPOS, per-site table sets (native Multisite isolation).
- Identity: network-global `wp_users` / `wp_usermeta` (shared login across halls).
- Bingo operational data: custom indexed `bc_*` tables — NEVER unindexed postmeta:
  sessions, availability rules, digital tickets/entitlements, redemption events,
  capacity counters (per-site); device registry, hall billing status, audit log,
  reporting facts (network-wide).

## Table Rules

- Per-site tables: `$wpdb->prefix . 'bc_<name>'` (auto-scoped to the hall).
- Network-wide tables: `$wpdb->base_prefix . 'bc_<name>'` and MUST include an
  indexed `blog_id` column.
- Every table has an indexed hall/site reference column. Common indexed columns:
  `blog_id`, `session_id`, `order_id`, `status`, `created_at`, `expires_at`,
  `token_hash`, `device_id`.
- Create/update via `dbDelta()` + a `bc_<table>_version` option for migrations.
  Migrations must be backward-aware and safe to run at network scale.

## Digital Ticket Table (canonical schema from technical-architecture.md)

Fields: `ticket_token` (unique, unguessable — store a hash where practical),
`order_id` (unique — ONE ticket per order, not per line item), `blog_id`,
`status` (`issued` / `redeemed` / `void`), `redeemed_device_id`, `redeemed_at`,
`reactivated_count`, `last_reactivated_at`, `last_reactivated_by_staff_id`.

## Capacity Counter (BR-025 — read this before touching checkout)

- Session capacity counts QUALIFYING PAID ORDERS, not packages. One order with
  any digital package(s) for the session consumes exactly ONE slot.
- An order containing packages for multiple sessions consumes one slot in EACH.
- Refunded/cancelled orders release their slot; pending/failed never count.
- Enforcement must be ATOMIC at checkout (e.g. conditional `UPDATE ... SET
  used = used + 1 WHERE used < cap` and check affected rows, or row locking)
  to prevent oversell under concurrent purchases. Read-then-write is a race
  condition and is rejected.
- Capacity value is configurable per session (default 300). NEVER hardcode 300.

## Reporting

- NEVER loop across hall sites/tables per request for platform reports. Write
  normalized network reporting facts in the background when orders change.
